@node "ErrorMsg" "TroubleShooting!"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "Main"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "ErrorMsg"}

 =========================================================================
             -  Error Messages (And What To Do About Them)  -
 =========================================================================

 This Util Is So Simple So I'm Sure There Won't Be Any Trouble With It
 But If You Ever Get One Of These Errors (Non Fatal) And You Wonderen What
 They Are All About...

 @{"Load Error #1 (ENViroment Statistix)"link "Error1"} @{"Load Error (Callerslog)             "link "Error3"}
 @{"Load Error #2 (ENViroment Statistix)"link "Error2"} @{"**Skipping; Local Sysop Login Entry!"link "Error4"}
                   
                   
@endnode

@node "Error1" "Load Error #1"
·Load Error #1 (ENViroment Statistix)
 ------------------------------------
 It Didn't Find The ENV:STATS<node> File That Is Allways Present When A
 User Has Logged Of The System.

 Cause: · You Have Run The Util Before The BBS Even Has Started Or
          Before You Got A Call.
@endnode
@node "Error2" "Load Error #2"
·Load Error #2 (ENViroment Statistix)
 ------------------------------------
 The ENV:STATS<node> file was empty!

 Cause: · You Probably Have Shutdown The BBS Before You Run The Util.

 What2Do: Make sure you run it directly after a user has logged off.
          Don't shutdown the BBS. You can check for yourself if the
          username is in the STAT file.
@endnode
@node "Error3" "Load Error Callerslog"
·Load Error (Callerslog)
 ------------------------------------
 Couldn't Process Callerslog For That Node.

 Cause: The Callerslog File Didn't Exist Or Couldn't Be Opened.
@endnode
@node "Error4" "**Skipping..."
·**Skipping; Local Sysop Login Entry!
 ------------------------------------
 Not An Error, You Have Specified NOSYSOP As An Argument And It Just
 Skip To Record The Last Call If It Was A SYSOP_LOCAL.
@endnode





